docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/reading-week-v2.md:571:- haiku-1 unmatched (11): e1: Singapore Police Force issued a prohibition of disposal order on a residence valued at about S$55 million ($42.4 million) and seized about S$1 million of funds in connection with fraud investigations. ‖ e2: Aaron Woon and Alan Wei were charged in February 2025 with criminal conspiracy to commit fraud, Li Ming was charged at the same time with fraud by false representation, and Jenny Lim was charged in April 2026. ‖ e4: Police charge Aperia Group defendants with conspiring to defraud Dell, Super Micro and Asus over server purchases, with false end-user representations made between November 2023 and February 2025. ‖ e5: Four companies in the case are due to face a total of eight fraud-by-false-representation charges to be announced on July 6, 2026, the first corporate prosecutions in these investigations. ‖ e6: Lim and Woon were each handed seven new charges, and Wei is set to receive seven new charges on July 6, 2026. ‖ e7: Police say Lim and Woon were each charged with money laundering after each acquired about SG$1.2 million in personal bank accounts, pointing to benefits from criminal conduct. ‖ e8: Wei faces three money laundering counts tied to the seized mansion and an additional S$5.8 (as printed) deposited in his personal account. ‖ e9: Li Ming faces additional fraud charges for misrepresenting the end-user of servers that Luxuriate Your Life intended to buy from Super Micro. ‖ e10: Malaysian authorities foiled an attempt to smuggle advanced AI chips through the main airport, seizing 72 servers worth nearly $13 million, in the week before the item. ‖ e11: Singaporean police say the number of such cases rose from 589 in H1 2024 to 1,762 in H1 2026, more than tripling. ‖ e12: Reports said in February 2025 that the U.S. Commerce Department was investigating whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia chips, possibly sourced via Malaysia and Singapore.
docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/loop-log.md:69:| 18 | 2026-10-30 | **验收结论**：五次同时全量（G、H、K、M、N）合起来 | — | 本次验收共 7,242 次，按公开价约 $8.2（$0.10/$0.50 每百万，缓存不打折，是上限） | 开发每次平均：核心三遍合计 v29 240.4、v42 238.4/258（各次差 −4、−10、−2、+4、+2）；核心三遍都留 74.8、73.6/86；辅助至少两遍 154.8、153.8/181；不收的被留每遍 139.8、102.8（−26%）；多留每遍 162.2、123.0（−24%）；必须开的问题每遍都开 17.6、18.6/28。测试：核心 8.2、8.4/9，辅助 38.2、37.8/42，不收的被留 53.0、40.4，多留 49.2、35.8。盲读（36 篇）：不收的被留 v42 114、v29 163；辅助达标 38、35/41 | v42 在"收哪些证据"上是这两天最好的，五次同时比较一致，盲读一致；**唯一的回归：给小产品、功能、服务的上线日期开问题**（每次全量约 15 个，主要是 DLSS 那一篇；v29 约 0）。两个修法（v49 去掉那句、v50 用 §6 原话）都让核心掉 3–5%，问题也没完全修好，都不留 | 交 Alex：换不换默认 |
docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md:69:- 量什么：问题页有多少、重复几个（读）；归位扔掉的"no home"逐条读（D209）；判断有没有因为证据太多出错停掉（D206 的原因：一个论点 1,768 条证据、292 KB 的请求）；每个论点视野里的证据数；花费和时间；和封存的三个月 v34 账本（到 08-28，69 个论点，$5.80）同日期段对比。
docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md:71:- 花费（估计）：按 v34 的 59 天 $5.80 推，全段 7–10 月约 $10–15，加上归位调用。
