**The plan would spend money before fixing what gets tested.** For example, the clean system would use the article exclusions, while production would still read its usual database. A difference in the final answers could come from different news rather than different systems. [Clean launcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:340) · [Production launcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:410)

1. **D665 and scope.** Move the blind matter census, cross-week grouping, and per-matter cutoffs to stage 0 and hash them **before the paid slice**. Stage 3 currently runs during the full replay, and stage 4 substitutes one end-date snapshot. Remove the four-week veto. D665 sets a minimum of 20 distinct matters and 30 distinct questions per system per draw, not a minimum number of weeks. Add the missing D400 reporting and hard checks, Step 2’s three measurements, the July 14 frozen-reference readout, and the source checks needed to report the proposed absolute floors. Naming those outputs in the report does not produce them. [Plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v1.md:97) · [Four-week veto](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v1.md:159) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9410) · [Step 2 measurements](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:338) · [Source checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:31)

2. **Launch blockers.**
   - **Articles and window.** An explicit manifest extends the launcher past July 14, but only the clean child consumes its IDs. The input helper compares sorted IDs, then hashes the clean list in production’s supplied order. It does not independently prove matching order or prove the production child honors exclusions. Make both entry points consume the same frozen selection and prove actual IDs, order, and text through both paths, including an excluded article. Include sources such as `poc/reports` and archived runs in the exposure census. The plan’s listed roots omit those records. [Window handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:429) · [Input helper](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh_week_inputs.py:43) · [Production input](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:319) · [Data manifest](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:33)
   - **Limits and astra.** Step 1 inherits **300 attempts and eight hours**, even on the shared ledger. Supply explicit, hashed comparison limits sized for the manifest and retries. The ladder child still sends with `SETTING` on luna. The parent checks only the first pass’s archive, after sending. Pass the named astra setting into the actual child, verify frozen request bytes before transport, and prove the intended passes and judge handoff. The judge consumes `send-1` only. Fix the other passes’ role in measuring stability and include their cost. These are required launcher changes beyond accepting a checksum. [Limits](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-limits.json:1) · [Enforcement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/live.py:82) · [Ladder setting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/stage_a.py:31) · [Actual send](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/stage_a.py:148) · [Ladder and judge handoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:379)
   - **Judge through the cutoff.** The child does not pass an end day, so the clean judge stops at the last article. Thread through the cutoff and prove closure on a trailing day with no articles. Exercise the existing judge on stored long-span input at $0 before launching. The historical long run halted on oversized evidence requests and refused citations. [Judge invocation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/run_stage_b.py:85) · [Calendar behavior](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/ladder_adapter.py:488) · [Historical halt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3791)

3. **Freeze the reading rules, not just the filenames.** A1 defines matter identity for one week. A2 maps one week’s openings and can mark a narrower or broader question as covering the main outcome. V1 cards only `opened` mappings. Before output, fix how those mappings earn credit, how readers settle cross-week identity, and whether the separate financial-figures row enters `N`. Freeze the guardrail sample and denominators, both split assignments, and verdict precedence. The controls also conflict: **3 of 4 supported and 2 of 3 repeats** versus **two of each per batch**. Fix which controls decide validity, exclude controls and repeats from product counts, and ensure a missed plant invalidates the reading. Rerun void sessions only, not valid marks that missed a plant. [A1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A1.md:9) · [A2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A2.md:10) · [Plan controls and scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v1.md:54) · [Batch and retry rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v1.md:115) · [Deck protocol](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/PROTOCOL.md:24)

4. **Make the stop executable.** `run.json` records component transitions, not article or day progress. Monitor trace and completed-day records directly. Define a stall by component, compare like draws at the same stage, and make the monitor stop the shared ledger. A stopped ledger refuses relaunches. Distinguish the launcher’s eligible component redo on a still-live ledger from a crash or shared stop. Also reconcile the slice’s “one failure allowed” with Step 1’s nonzero exit for `complete_with_failures`. [Launcher state and redo](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/run_fresh.py:238) · [Ledger stop](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:212) · [Step 1 exit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/run_live.py:41)

5. **Rebase the 1.5× check before using it.** The recorded July slice took **7m23s for 13 clean articles**, about **34 seconds each**, already above v1’s implied **22.5-second** stop. The old-system price comes from v34, despite available v118 measurements. Freeze separate baselines using the actual manifest and comparable component traces. Price astra by sends and retries, and include concurrent reservations when checking the $250 guard. A short slice checks wiring and early costs. It does not establish late judge cost. [V1 estimates](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v1.md:133) · [Measured slice and v118 estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/SLICE-RESULT.md:8) · [Astra pricing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/gate1-candidate/gate1_candidate.py:69)

**NOT READY: freeze the census and verdict before the slice, prove both launchers on the same inputs through the cutoff, restore D665’s required checks, and set enforceable stops using comparable cost and timing records.**
